notes.content:
Well, it sure has been a while.

https://clan.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/41029023/78d01dd0f27d5ab1ac83833c64ee9509fa5729a0.png

We're happy to announce the release of the final(?) Printersim update entitled The Nightmare Update. This bad boy is retrofitted with the hottest new holistic bells & whistles, with the most exciting up-front:

 A whole new [strike]nightmare[/strike] innovative business meeting to experience;
 A fancy menu to revisit those memories we made along the way;
 A variety of quality of life changes;
 Various unprofitable bug-fixes;
 Boring Corporate Boilerplate (BCB);
 Hints;
 Even more hints.

Some of the updates are tied to achievements, so you may want to go exploring again :)

And for those that wish to re-experience the demo, we've created a beta-branch just for that so check it out!

Now for those that love reading fine-print, EULAs, or even political manifestos, then please look below for a full breakdown of the changes.

Change Logs

Features

 A whole new nightmare to experience (it's tied to an achievement);
 Added a nightmare menu for revisiting cutscenes and one of the endings;
 It is now possible to lock the mouse to the window via the options menu;
 Some cutscenes (if already seen) can be skipped with a right-click.

Changes

 Changed the copyright notice to match our company name;
 Added a prompt to the "how to play" to reassure players;
 Computer icons will now open up applications even if minimised;
 Adjusted audio levels of some sounds and music to that overall volume is more consistent;
 Stopped some unnecessary temporary files for error logging;
 Changed some of the names in the credits.

Bug Fixes

 Stop sounds from trying to play multiple times;
 Removed "inventory full" message after [spoiler]fighting the Printer for the final report[/spoiler]. Turns out this was because the game was trying to re-add the player's trophies after each attempt.
